Z||000006||theogre||08-11-99||02:23 PM||||Actually there are small enough turbine engines that fit in a car. Currently they are being used as part of hybrid electric setups. The turbine runs a generator that can charge the batteries, and/or, run the electic motor in the car.<p>There is enough space in the back of a Fiero that it could be done. If you did a turbine electric one w/o the battery bank, it would probably weigh about the same as the V6, and blow the doors off many v8's. <p>To bad a straight jet wouldn't be street legal. That would make a cool looking drag car. There are some pretty small jet engines around...... May be a pair with the driver between them, like ThrustSSC ran.
